#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:5
msgid "強誘電性と結晶構造"
msgstr "Ferroelectricity and Crystal Structure"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:7
msgid ""
"強誘電体は、\\ :ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ "
"をもち、外部電場によってその向きを反転できる物質である。 代表例のチタン酸バリウム（BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"）を通して、結晶の対称性と 原子変位がどのように分極につながるかを見ていく。"
msgstr ""
"A ferroelectric is a material that has \\ :ref:`spontaneous polarization "
"<spontaneous-polarization>` \\ whose direction can be reversed by an "
"external electric field. Using the representative example of barium "
"titanate (BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ ), we examine how crystal symmetry and "
"atomic displacements give rise to polarization."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:11
msgid ""
"ここでは、結晶構造から強誘電性を理解するための基本を扱う。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の "
"計算条件やQuloudでの操作手順は扱わない。具体的な計算事例と操作手順は、 それぞれQuloud "
"Examplesとオンラインマニュアルで扱う。周期結晶の分極の値の求め方は「\\ :ref:`periodic-polarization`\\ "
"」、 立方晶が極性の変位に対して不安定になる理由は「\\ :ref:`ferroelectric-origin`\\ "
"」で扱う。自由エネルギーの展開からの導出は 「\\ :ref:`landau-theory`\\ 」にまとめた。"
msgstr ""
"This article covers the basics of understanding ferroelectricity from "
"crystal structure. The calculation settings for BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ and "
"the steps for using Quloud are outside its scope. Quloud Examples "
"provides specific calculation examples, and the online manual covers the "
"operating procedures. For how to calculate polarization in periodic "
"crystals, see \\ :ref:`Polarization in Periodic Crystals <periodic-"
"polarization>`\\ . For why the cubic structure is unstable against polar "
"displacements, see \\ :ref:`Origin of the Ferroelectric Instability of "
"BaTiO₃ <ferroelectric-origin>`\\ . The derivation from a free-energy "
"expansion is given in \\ :ref:`Landau Theory and the Order of Phase "
"Transitions <landau-theory>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:17
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`反転対称性と自発分極<inversion-and-polarization>`、:ref:`等価な方向の族"
"<equivalent-directions>`、:ref:`ペロブスカイトの擬立方格子<pseudocubic-"
"cell>`、:ref:`ソフトモードと構造相転移<soft-mode>`\\ （とくに\\ :ref:`秩序変数としてのモードの振幅<sm-"
"landau>`）、:ref:`Landau理論と相転移の次数<landau-theory>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Inversion symmetry and spontaneous polarization "
"<inversion-and-polarization>`, :ref:`families of equivalent directions "
"<equivalent-directions>`, the :ref:`pseudocubic lattice of perovskites "
"<pseudocubic-cell>`, :ref:`soft modes and structural phase transitions "
"<soft-mode>` \\ (especially \\ :ref:`mode amplitude as an order parameter"
" <sm-landau>`), and :ref:`Landau theory and the order of phase "
"transitions <landau-theory>`."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:19
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:21
msgid ""
"常誘電相の誘電率がCurie–Weissの法則に従うことと、1次転移では転移温度とCurie–Weiss温度がずれることを説明し、BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ の二重ヒステリシスの観測から転移の次数を読む。"
msgstr ""
"Explain that the permittivity of the paraelectric phase follows the "
"Curie–Weiss law and that the transition temperature differs from the "
"Curie–Weiss temperature for a first-order transition. Use the observed "
"double hysteresis in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ to identify the order of the "
"transition."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:22
msgid "BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の4つの相の空間群と分極の向きを、擬立方格子の方向で説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Describe the space groups and polarization directions of the four BaTiO\\"
" :sub:`3` \\ phases using pseudocubic lattice directions."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:23
msgid "分極の方位状態の数（分域がとりうる分極の向きの数）を点群の位数から求め、隣り合う分域の分極がなす角を挙げる。"
msgstr ""
"Determine the number of polarization orientation states (the number of "
"possible polarization directions of a domain) from the orders of the "
"point groups. List the angles between the polarizations of neighboring "
"domains."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:24
msgid "回折で決まる平均構造と、各単位胞の局所的な変位の違いを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain how the average structure determined by diffraction differs from "
"the local displacements in individual unit cells."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:30
msgid "自発分極と強誘電性"
msgstr "Spontaneous Polarization and Ferroelectricity"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:32
msgid ""
"分極は、電気双極子モーメントを体積で割った量であり、単位体積あたりの 電荷の偏りを表す。結晶では、正負のイオンの変位に加えて電子密度の変化も "
"分極に寄与する。"
msgstr ""
"Polarization is electric dipole moment per unit volume and describes the "
"charge imbalance per unit volume. In a crystal, changes in the electron "
"density contribute to polarization as well as displacements of positive "
"and negative ions."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:36
msgid ""
"結晶構造が極性をもつと、自発分極が許される。ただし、極性があることだけで 強誘電体とは限らない。強誘電体と呼ぶには、自発分極の向きを外部電場で "
"可逆に切り替えられることが必要である。"
msgstr ""
"A polar crystal structure allows spontaneous polarization. Polarity "
"alone, however, does not guarantee ferroelectricity. For a material to be"
" ferroelectric, its spontaneous polarization must be reversibly "
"switchable by an external electric field."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:44
msgid "常誘電相とキュリー温度"
msgstr "Paraelectric Phase and the Curie Temperature"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:46
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"強誘電体を加熱すると、ある温度で自発分極が消え、電場をかけている間だけ分極が生じる相に移る。 この高温の相を\\ **常誘電相**\\ "
"（paraelectric phase）、転移温度を\\ **キュリー温度** :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` と呼ぶ（\\ "
":ref:`ソフトモードの記事<sm-definition>`\\ の転移温度 :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}` "
"にあたる）。常誘電相では、弱い電場 :math:`E` に比例して分極が生じ、 電気感受率 :math:`\\chi` を使って "
":math:`P=\\varepsilon_0\\chi E` と書ける。強誘電体の常誘電相では、 :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` "
"に近づくと :math:`\\chi` が大きくなり、"
msgstr ""
"On heating a ferroelectric, spontaneous polarization vanishes at a "
"certain temperature. The crystal enters a phase in which polarization "
"appears only while an electric field is applied. This high-temperature "
"phase is called the \\ **paraelectric phase**\\ , and the transition "
"temperature is the \\ **Curie temperature** :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` (the "
"\\ :ref:`transition temperature <sm-definition>` \\  denoted by "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm c}` in the soft-mode article). In the paraelectric "
"phase the polarization is proportional to a weak electric field "
":math:`E`. With electric susceptibility :math:`\\chi`, it is "
":math:`P=\\varepsilon_0\\chi E`. In the paraelectric phase of a "
"ferroelectric, as the temperature approaches :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, "
":math:`\\chi` increases according to"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:52
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\chi=\\frac{C}{T-T_0}"
msgstr "\\chi=\\frac{C}{T-T_0}"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:57
msgid ""
"に従う。これを\\ **Curie–Weissの法則**\\ 、:math:`C` をCurie定数、:math:`T_0` "
"をCurie–Weiss温度と呼ぶ。:ref:`極性ソフトモード<polar-soft-mode>`\\ "
"の振動数が下がると静的な誘電率が発散するので、 この法則は格子振動の側からも導ける。その場合の :math:`T_0` は、Cochranの法則 "
":eq:`sm-cochran` でソフトモードの振動数が0に外挿される温度である。 分極で展開した自由エネルギーからの導出は\\ "
":ref:`共役な場への応答<landau-curie-weiss>`\\ にある。"
msgstr ""
"This is the \\ **Curie–Weiss law**\\ , with Curie constant :math:`C` and "
"Curie–Weiss temperature :math:`T_0`. As the frequency of the :ref:`polar "
"soft mode <polar-soft-mode>` \\ decreases, the static permittivity "
"diverges, so this law can also be derived from lattice vibrations. In "
"that derivation, :math:`T_0` is the temperature at which extrapolation by"
" Cochran's law in Equation :eq:`sm-cochran` gives zero soft-mode "
"frequency. For a derivation from a free-energy expansion in polarization,"
" see \\ :ref:`the response to a conjugate field <landau-curie-weiss>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`T_0` と :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` の関係は、分極で展開した自由エネルギーから分かる "
"[Devonshire1949]_。導出は 「\\ :ref:`landau-theory`\\ "
"」で扱い、ここでは結論だけを述べる。分極の4次の係数が正なら、分極は :math:`T_0` から連続的に育つ \\ :ref:`2次転移"
"<second-order-transition>`\\ になり、:math:`T_{\\mathrm C}=T_0` "
"である。4次の係数が負なら\\ :ref:`1次転移<first-order-transition>`\\ になり、 分極は "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` で有限の値へ跳び、常誘電相の :math:`\\chi` から外挿した :math:`T_0` は "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` より低い。1次転移では、 冷却と加熱で常誘電相と強誘電相がそれぞれ\\ "
":ref:`準安定な状態として残りうる<landau-metastability>`\\ ので、転移温度が加熱と冷却でずれうる。"
msgstr ""
"The relationship between :math:`T_0` and :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` follows "
"from the free energy expanded in polarization [Devonshire1949]_. See \\ "
":ref:`Landau Theory and the Order of Phase Transitions <landau-theory>` "
"\\ for the derivation. Here we give only the conclusions. If the quartic "
"coefficient in polarization is positive, polarization grows continuously "
"from :math:`T_0` in a \\ :ref:`second-order transition <second-order-"
"transition>`\\ , and :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}=T_0`. If the quartic "
"coefficient is negative, there is a \\ :ref:`first-order transition "
"<first-order-transition>`\\ . Polarization jumps to a finite value at "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, and extrapolation of :math:`\\chi` from the "
"paraelectric phase gives :math:`T_0` below :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`. In a "
"first-order transition, the paraelectric phase on cooling and the "
"ferroelectric phase on heating can \\ :ref:`persist as metastable states "
"<landau-metastability>`\\ , so the transition temperatures on heating and"
" cooling may differ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、Merzが :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}` "
"のすぐ上で、弱い電場では直線、強い電場では両端に ヒステリシスが開く分極–電場曲線（二重ヒステリシス）を観測し、4次の係数が負であること、 "
"つまり立方晶から正方晶への転移が1次であることを示した [Merz1953]_\\ （\\ :ref:`読み方<landau-"
"batio3-example>`）。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の三つの転移は いずれも1次である [Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"In BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , just above :math:`T_{\\mathrm C}`, Merz observed "
"a polarization–electric field curve that was linear at weak fields but "
"opened into hysteresis loops at the two ends at strong fields (double "
"hysteresis). This showed that the quartic coefficient is negative, which "
"identifies the cubic-to-tetragonal transition as first order [Merz1953]_ "
"\\ (see \\ :ref:`interpretation of the data <landau-batio3-example>`). "
"All three transitions in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ are first order "
"[Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:76
msgid "BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の立方晶相と正方晶相"
msgstr "Cubic and Tetragonal Phases of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:78
msgid ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ は、理想的なペロブスカイト構造をもつ。高温の立方晶相では、 "
"平均構造としてTi原子が周囲の6個の酸素原子が作る八面体の中心に位置する。この構造には :ref:`反転中心<inversion-and-"
"polarization>`\\ があり、結晶全体として特定の向きの自発分極は生じない。 立方晶相はBaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "
"の常誘電相である。"
msgstr ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ has the ideal perovskite structure. In the average "
"structure of the high-temperature cubic phase, each Ti atom lies at the "
"center of the octahedron formed by its six oxygen neighbors. This "
"structure has a :ref:`center of inversion <inversion-and-polarization>`\\"
" , so the crystal as a whole develops no spontaneous polarization along "
"any particular direction. For BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ the cubic phase is the "
"paraelectric phase."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:83
msgid ""
"バルクのBaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ を冷却すると、約393 Kで立方晶相から正方晶相へ移る。 "
"正方晶相ではTiと酸素の相対位置が変わり、反転対称性が失われる。結晶の 長軸方向に極性が生じ、自発分極をもつ。この構造変化が強誘電性の起源を "
"理解するための基本例となる [Zhong1995]_ [Bull2021]_。"
msgstr ""
"On cooling, bulk BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ changes from the cubic phase to the "
"tetragonal phase at about 393 K. In the tetragonal phase, the relative "
"positions of Ti and oxygen change and inversion symmetry is lost. The "
"crystal becomes polar along its long axis and has spontaneous "
"polarization. This structural change is a basic example for understanding"
" the origin of ferroelectricity [Zhong1995]_ [Bull2021]_."

