#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:192
msgid "4つの立方体。左から立方晶は中心の点だけ、正方晶は面の中心へ向かう001の矢印、直方晶は辺の中点へ向かう011の矢印、菱面体晶は頂点へ向かう111の矢印。同じ族の他の方向を灰色の点で示す。"
msgstr ""
"Four cubes from left to right: the cubic phase with just a central dot, "
"the tetragonal phase with a [001] arrow to a face center, the "
"orthorhombic phase with a [011] arrow to an edge midpoint, and the "
"rhombohedral phase with a [111] arrow to a vertex. Gray dots indicate the"
" other directions in each family."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:198
msgid ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の4相の分極の向き。左から高温側の順に並べた。立方体は擬立方胞、中央の点はTiの平均位置を表す。 "
"矢印は分極の向きの一例で、正方晶は面の中心、直方晶は辺の中点、菱面体晶は頂点へ向かう。 "
"灰色の点は、立方晶の対称操作で矢印の向きと移り合う方向（同じ族の残りの方向）を示す。破線は奥に隠れた辺である。"
msgstr ""
"Polarization directions in the four phases of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , from "
"highest to lowest temperature. The cubes represent pseudocubic cells, "
"with the average Ti position marked at the center. Each arrow shows a "
"representative polarization direction: toward a face center in the "
"tetragonal phase, toward an edge midpoint in the orthorhombic phase, and "
"toward a vertex in the rhombohedral phase. Gray dots indicate the other "
"directions in each family, related to the arrow direction by cubic "
"symmetry operations. Dashed lines mark hidden back edges."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:202
msgid ""
"表の最後の列は、相を見分ける指標になる。\\ :ref:`等価な方向の族<equivalent-directions>`\\ "
"で見たとおり、立方晶の点群 :math:`m\\bar3m` "
"の操作は、分極の成分の並べ替えと符号の反転である。これらの操作で、どの軸の成分が0でないかや "
"その符号は変わるが、0でない成分の数は変わらない。したがって、次節の分域のどれを選んでも、0でない成分の数は相ごとに3・2・1・0の決まった値になる。"
" `計算事例「構造相転移」 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html#batio3-phase-"
"distributions>`_\\ も、Tiの変位の分布で、0からずれたピークをもつ軸の数を\\ :ref:`相の判定<heating-"
"phase-indicators>`\\ に使っている。ただし、反対向きの分域が同じ領域に "
"混じっていると、平均した成分は打ち消し合う。この指標は、一つの分域の中で平均した変位に使う。"
msgstr ""
"The number of nonzero polarization components in the last column can help"
" identify the phase. As in \\ :ref:`families of equivalent directions "
"<equivalent-directions>`\\ , operations of the cubic point group "
":math:`m\\bar3m` permute polarization components and reverse their signs."
" These operations can change which components are nonzero and what their "
"signs are, but they leave the number of nonzero components unchanged. "
"Thus, whichever domain from the next section is chosen, the number of "
"nonzero components has a fixed value for each phase (3, 2, 1, or 0). The "
"`calculation example “Structural Phase Transitions” <https://example"
".quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html#batio3-phase-"
"distributions>`_ \\ also uses the number of axes with peaks displaced "
"from zero in the Ti displacement distribution \\ :ref:`to identify the "
"phase <heating-phase-indicators>`\\ . However, if oppositely oriented "
"domains are mixed within the same region, their components cancel on "
"averaging. Apply this indicator to displacements averaged within a single"
" domain."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:208
msgid ""
"分極をもつ3つの相では、どれも格子が分極の方向に伸びている。正方晶では :math:`c>a`、直方晶では極性軸に沿う胞の辺が "
"垂直な辺より長く（\\ :ref:`直方晶の胞との換算<pseudocubic-"
"orthorhombic>`）、菱面体晶では擬立方胞の角が90°よりわずかに小さく（約89.8° [Kwei1993]_）、 "
":math:`[111]` 方向に伸びた形になる。Merzは、正方晶の変形が自発分極の2乗に比例することを示した [Merz1949]_。 "
"どの向きが最も低いエネルギーを与えるかは、立方晶の対称性が許す4次以上の項で決まる（式 :eq:`sm-cubic-quartic`）。"
msgstr ""
"In each of the three phases with polarization, the lattice is elongated "
"along the polarization direction. In the tetragonal phase, :math:`c>a`. "
"In the orthorhombic phase, the cell edge along the polar axis is longer "
"than the perpendicular edge (see \\ :ref:`conversion to the orthorhombic "
"cell <pseudocubic-orthorhombic>`). In the rhombohedral phase, the angles "
"of the pseudocubic cell are slightly less than 90° (about 89.8° "
"[Kwei1993]_), giving an elongation along :math:`[111]`. Merz showed that "
"the tetragonal distortion is proportional to the square of the "
"spontaneous polarization [Merz1949]_. Which direction gives the lowest "
"energy is determined by the terms of fourth and higher order allowed by "
"cubic symmetry (Equation :eq:`sm-cubic-quartic`)."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:217
msgid "分域と分域壁"
msgstr "Domains and Domain Walls"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:219
msgid ""
"電場やひずみがなく、結晶が立方晶の対称性を保つ条件では、分極が族の中のどの方向を向いてもエネルギーは等しい。立方晶の対称操作で移り合う向きは、:ref:`+Qと−Qの等価性"
"<sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\ と同じ理由で、同じエネルギーをもつからである。 "
"このエネルギーの等しい向きの数は、点群の位数（操作の数）から求められる。立方晶の点群 :math:`G=m\\bar3m` の48個の操作のうち、"
" 選んだ分極の向きを変えない操作の集まりは、低温相の点群 :math:`F` になる。正方晶の :math:`[001]` を変えないのは、 "
":math:`z` 軸のまわりの回転と、:math:`z` 軸を含む鏡映の8個（:math:`4mm`）である。:math:`G` の残りの操作は"
" :math:`[001]` を別の向きへ移し、同じ向きへ移す操作は :math:`F` の位数だけある。したがって、向きの数は"
msgstr ""
"In the absence of electric field and strain, under conditions that "
"preserve cubic symmetry, the energy is the same for all polarization "
"directions in a family. Directions related by cubic symmetry operations "
"have equal energies for the same reason that :ref:`+Q and −Q are "
"equivalent <sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\ . The number of equal-energy "
"directions follows from the orders (numbers of operations) of the point "
"groups. Of the 48 operations of the cubic point group :math:`G=m\\bar3m`,"
" those that leave the chosen polarization direction unchanged form the "
"point group :math:`F` of the low-temperature phase. For the tetragonal "
"direction :math:`[001]`, eight operations leave it unchanged: rotations "
"about the :math:`z` axis and reflections in planes containing the "
":math:`z` axis (:math:`4mm`). The remaining operations of :math:`G` take "
":math:`[001]` to other directions, with as many operations yielding each "
"direction as the order of :math:`F`. The number of directions is "
"therefore"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:225
#, python-brace-format
msgid "n=\\frac{|G|}{|F|}"
msgstr "n=\\frac{|G|}{|F|}"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:230
msgid ""
"で、正方晶 :math:`48/8=6`、直方晶 :math:`48/4=12`、菱面体晶 :math:`48/6=8` "
"となり、:math:`\\langle100\\rangle`・ "
":math:`\\langle110\\rangle`・:math:`\\langle111\\rangle` "
"の族の方向の数に一致する（:numref:`fig-batio3-polar-directions`\\ "
"の点の数）。Aizuは、このように対称性の高い相から生じる同等な状態を方位状態（orientation state）と呼び、強誘電体などを分類した"
" [Aizu1970]_。"
msgstr ""
"This gives :math:`48/8=6` for the tetragonal phase, :math:`48/4=12` for "
"the orthorhombic phase, and :math:`48/6=8` for the rhombohedral phase. "
"These are the numbers of directions in the :math:`\\langle100\\rangle`, "
":math:`\\langle110\\rangle`, and :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` families, "
"respectively (the numbers of dots in :numref:`fig-batio3-polar-"
"directions`\\ ). Aizu called these equivalent states arising from a "
"higher-symmetry phase orientation states and used them to classify "
"ferroelectrics and other materials [Aizu1970]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:233
msgid ""
"どの向きもエネルギーが等しいので、電場をかけずに冷やした結晶では、場所ごとに異なる向きが選ばれうる。分極の向きがそろった領域を\\ "
"**分域**\\ （ドメイン）、 その境界を\\ **分域壁**\\ と呼ぶ。:eq:`fe-domain-count` の :math:`n` "
"は分域がとりうる向き（方位状態）の数で、実際に現れる分域の数や体積の割合は、 "
"表面や電極の状態、応力、冷却の履歴などにも依存する。隣り合う分域の分極がなす角は、二つの方向ベクトルの内積から求まり、相によって決まった値をとる。"
msgstr ""
"Because the directions have equal energies, different regions of a "
"crystal may choose different directions on cooling in zero field. A "
"region with a uniform polarization direction is a \\ **domain**\\ , and "
"the boundary is a \\ **domain wall**\\ . In Equation :eq:`fe-domain-"
"count`, :math:`n` is the number of possible directions (orientation "
"states) for a domain. The actual number and volume fractions of domains "
"also depend on the surfaces and electrodes, stress, cooling history, and "
"other factors. The angle between neighboring domains' polarizations "
"follows from the dot product of their direction vectors and takes "
"specific values for each phase."

