#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:255
msgid ""
"180°の分域壁を挟む二つの分域は、分極の符号だけが異なり、格子の伸びる方向は同じである。 "
"それ以外の分域壁では、格子が伸びる方向も変わる。正方晶の90°分域壁では、両側で :math:`c` 軸の向きが90°異なる。"
msgstr ""
"The two domains across a 180° domain wall differ only in the sign of "
"their polarization and have the same direction of lattice elongation. "
"Across other domain walls, the direction of elongation also changes. At a"
" tetragonal 90° domain wall, the :math:`c` axis changes orientation by "
"90° across the wall."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:258
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"分域ができる理由の一つは、表面に現れる電荷である。分極 :math:`\\boldsymbol P` の結晶の表面（外向きの法線 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol n`）には、 面密度 :math:`\\boldsymbol P\\cdot\\boldsymbol n`"
" の分極電荷が現れる。分極に垂直な板状の結晶で、表面の電荷を打ち消す電荷が外から 供給されないと、内部では電束密度 "
":math:`D=\\varepsilon_0E+P` が0になり、:math:`E=-P/\\varepsilon_0` の電場が生じる "
"（電子の分極による遮蔽は無視した）。:math:`P=0.26\\ \\mathrm{C/m^2}` なら "
":math:`|E|\\simeq3\\times10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{V/m}` である。 電場のエネルギー密度 "
":math:`\\varepsilon_0E^2/2=P^2/(2\\varepsilon_0)` は、化学式単位の体積（約64 Å\\ "
":sup:`3`）あたり約1.5 eVで、 立方晶から極性の構造へ移って下がるエネルギー（転移温度の熱エネルギー程度 "
"[CohenKrakauer1990]_）より桁違いに大きい。逆向きの分域が交互に並ぶか、電極や吸着物が表面の電荷を打ち消すと、この電場は小さくなる。"
msgstr ""
"One reason domains form is the charge that appears at the surface. For a "
"crystal with polarization :math:`\\boldsymbol P`, a surface with outward "
"normal :math:`\\boldsymbol n` has bound polarization charge per area "
":math:`\\boldsymbol P\\cdot\\boldsymbol n`. In a plate with surfaces "
"perpendicular to the polarization, if no external charges are supplied to"
" compensate the surface charge, the electric displacement "
":math:`D=\\varepsilon_0E+P` vanishes in the interior and an electric "
"field :math:`E=-P/\\varepsilon_0` develops (neglecting screening by "
"electronic polarization). For :math:`P=0.26\\ \\mathrm{C/m^2}`, "
":math:`|E|\\simeq3\\times10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{V/m}`. The electric field "
"energy density :math:`\\varepsilon_0E^2/2=P^2/(2\\varepsilon_0)` amounts "
"to about 1.5 eV per formula-unit volume (about 64 Å\\ :sup:`3`), orders "
"of magnitude larger than the energy gained on going from the cubic to the"
" polar structure (on the order of the thermal energy at the transition "
"temperature [CohenKrakauer1990]_). The field is reduced if oppositely "
"oriented domains alternate or if electrodes or adsorbates compensate the "
"surface charge."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:265
msgid ""
"電場をかけると、電場の向きに近い分極をもつ分域が広がり、結晶全体の分極が反転する。Merzは、BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の単結晶で "
"分極を反転させるとき、既存の180°分域壁が横に動くことはまれで、逆向きの薄い分域が多数生まれ、主に分極の方向へ伸びて "
"反転が進むことを観察した。分域壁の厚さは格子定数の1〜数倍と見積もられている [Merz1954]_。"
msgstr ""
"When an electric field is applied, domains with polarization closer to "
"the field direction grow, and the overall crystal polarization reverses. "
"When reversing polarization in single-crystal BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , Merz "
"observed that preexisting 180° domain walls rarely moved sideways. "
"Instead, many thin domains with opposite polarization formed and grew "
"mainly along the polarization direction as reversal progressed. The wall "
"thickness is estimated at one to a few lattice constants [Merz1954]_."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:269
msgid ""
"周期境界条件の小さな胞の計算では、胞の中で分極の向きが一つにそろい、一つの分域だけからなる結晶を表す。 "
"分域壁を含む構造を調べるには、壁を収める大きさの超胞が要る。"
msgstr ""
"A calculation with periodic boundary conditions and a small cell "
"represents a single-domain crystal with one polarization direction "
"throughout the cell. To study a structure containing a domain wall, use a"
" supercell large enough to accommodate the wall."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:276
msgid "説明用の事例：局所的なTiの変位と平均構造"
msgstr "Worked Example: Local Ti Displacements and Average Structure"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:278
msgid ""
"Bragg反射の回折で決まる構造は、空間と時間について平均した\\ **平均構造**\\ である。各単位胞の瞬間的な原子配置 "
"（局所構造）は、散漫散乱、\\ :ref:`二体分布関数<radial-distribution-function>`\\ "
"（PDF）、X線吸収微細構造（XAFS）などで調べる。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、 以下の測定が示すように、両者が一致しない。"
msgstr ""
"Bragg diffraction measures the \\ **average structure** \\ in space and "
"time. Diffuse scattering, the \\ :ref:`pair distribution function "
"<radial-distribution-function>` \\ (PDF), and X-ray absorption fine "
"structure (XAFS), among other techniques, probe the instantaneous atomic "
"configuration (local structure) of individual unit cells. In BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ , the two structures differ, as the following measurements "
"show."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:282
msgid ""
"二つの描像がある "
"[Shi2018]_。変位型の描像では、Tiは各相の分極の向きに変位し、立方晶相では八面体の中心にいる。8サイト模型と呼ばれる秩序–無秩序型の描像では、どの相でもTiは八面体の中心から8つの"
" :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` 方向の どれかにずれており、相ごとにその選び方の偏りが違う "
"[Bersuker1966]_ [Comes1968]_。変位を :math:`(\\pm d,\\pm d,\\pm d)` と書くと、 "
"菱面体晶相では全ての胞が同じ符号の組を選ぶ。直方晶相では2成分の符号がそろい、残る1成分の符号が胞ごとに "
"ばらばらなので、その成分は平均すると0になり、平均の変位は :math:`\\langle110\\rangle` を向く。正方晶相では "
"そろう成分が1つ、立方晶相では0個である。平均の変位の0でない成分の数3・2・1・0は、ここではそろった符号の数として現れ、 "
"変位型の描像と同じ平均構造を与える。二つの描像は、局所構造で区別される。"
msgstr ""
"Two pictures describe the Ti displacements [Shi2018]_. In the displacive "
"picture, Ti shifts in the polarization direction of each phase and is at "
"the center of the octahedron in the cubic phase. In the order–disorder "
"picture, called the eight-site model, Ti is displaced from the octahedron"
" center in one of eight :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` directions in every "
"phase, with a different preference among those directions in each phase "
"[Bersuker1966]_ [Comes1968]_. Writing the displacement as :math:`(\\pm "
"d,\\pm d,\\pm d)`, all cells in the rhombohedral phase choose the same "
"combination of signs. In the orthorhombic phase, the signs of two "
"components are aligned, but the sign of the third varies from cell to "
"cell. That component averages to zero, so the mean displacement points "
"along a :math:`\\langle110\\rangle` direction. In the tetragonal phase "
"one component aligns, and in the cubic phase none do. The counts of "
"nonzero mean displacement components (3, 2, 1, and 0) are the numbers of "
"aligned signs in this picture, yielding the same average structures as "
"the displacive picture. Local structure distinguishes the two pictures."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:289
msgid ""
"Comèsらは、Tiの変位が鎖状に相関すると考えると説明できる散漫散乱を観測した [Comes1968]_ （鎖状にそろいやすい理由は\\ "
":ref:`双極子どうしの相互作用<ferroelectric-instability-"
"origin>`）。Sennらは、PDFの解析から、Tiの局所的な変位が既知のすべての相で菱面体晶的（:math:`\\langle111\\rangle`"
" 方向に近い）であることを示した。 局所的な変位の相関だけを入れたモンテカルロ模型で相の順序を再現し、秩序–無秩序型の描像を支持しつつ、 "
"ソフトモードの描像とも両立しうると述べている [Senn2016]_。XAFSでも、変位型と秩序–無秩序型の成分が共存すると報告されている "
"[Stern2004]_。どちらの成分がどれだけ寄与するかの一般論は、\\ :ref:`変位型と秩序–無秩序型の相転移<displacive-"
"order-disorder>`\\ にある。"
msgstr ""
"Comès and coauthors observed diffuse scattering that can be explained by "
"chain-like correlations of Ti displacements [Comes1968]_ (the tendency to"
" align in chains follows from \\ :ref:`dipole–dipole interactions "
"<ferroelectric-instability-origin>`). Senn and coauthors used PDF "
"analysis to show that the local Ti displacements are rhombohedral-like "
"(close to :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` directions) in all known phases. A "
"Monte Carlo model using only correlations between local displacements "
"reproduced the phase sequence. They argued that this supports the "
"order–disorder picture but is also compatible with the soft-mode picture "
"[Senn2016]_. XAFS measurements also indicate that displacive and "
"order–disorder components coexist [Stern2004]_. For a general discussion "
"of their relative contributions, see \\ :ref:`displacive and "
"order–disorder phase transitions <displacive-order-disorder>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:295
msgid ""
"このことから、立方晶の平均構造 :math:`Pm\\bar3m` は、ある瞬間の原子配置ではない。有限温度の\\ :ref:`分子動力学法"
"<molecular-dynamics>`\\ の "
"スナップショットでは、立方晶相でもTiは中心からずれ、平均を取って初めて立方晶の対称性が現れる。0 Kの\\ :ref:`構造最適化"
"<structure-optimization>`\\ で 対称性を課した立方晶は、極性の変位に対して不安定な\\ :ref:`鞍点の構造"
"<phonon-batio3-example>`\\ である。0 "
"Kの計算は、局所的な極性不安定性がなぜ生じるかを調べるのに向き、その変位が温度とともにどうそろい、 どう乱れるかは\\ :ref:`有限温度の計算"
"<apparent-transition-temperature>`\\ で調べる。"
msgstr ""
"These results show that the cubic average structure :math:`Pm\\bar3m` is "
"not an instantaneous atomic configuration. In snapshots from finite-"
"temperature \\ :ref:`molecular dynamics <molecular-dynamics>`\\ , Ti is "
"off-center even in the cubic phase. Cubic symmetry emerges only after "
"averaging. In \\ :ref:`structure optimization <structure-optimization>` "
"\\ at 0 K, the symmetry-constrained cubic structure is a \\ :ref:`saddle-"
"point structure <phonon-batio3-example>` \\ unstable against polar "
"displacements. Calculations at 0 K help explain why the local polar "
"instability occurs. Use \\ :ref:`finite-temperature calculations "
"<apparent-transition-temperature>` \\ to study how these displacements "
"develop or lose alignment as temperature changes."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:304
msgid "構造最適化の結果を読むとき"
msgstr "Interpreting Structure Optimization Results"

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:306
msgid ""
"立方晶構造と正方晶構造をそれぞれ計算し、全エネルギーや原子位置を比較すると、 "
"どちらの構造が計算条件のもとで安定かを調べられる。原子位置の変化からは、 対称性が保たれているか、極性を生む変位が現れているかを確認できる。"
msgstr ""
"Calculating the cubic and tetragonal structures separately and comparing "
"their total energies and atomic positions shows which structure is stable"
" under the calculation conditions. Changes in the atomic positions show "
"whether symmetry is preserved and whether displacements that produce "
"polarity appear."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:310
msgid ""
"ただし、ゼロ温度近似の\\ :ref:`構造最適化<structure-optimization>`\\ "
"だけで、実験で観測される温度ごとの相転移を 再現したことにはならない。相転移温度や相の安定性には、有限温度での振動や "
"エントロピーなども関わる。また、構造が極性を許すことと、電場で分極を反転 できることは別の性質である。"
msgstr ""
"However, \\ :ref:`structure optimization <structure-optimization>` \\ in "
"the zero-temperature approximation alone does not reproduce the phase "
"transitions observed experimentally as a function of temperature. Finite-"
"temperature vibrations, entropy, and other effects contribute to "
"transition temperatures and phase stability. A structure that allows "
"polarity and the ability to reverse its polarization with an electric "
"field are also distinct properties."

#: ../../solid/ferroelectricity.rst:315
msgid ""
"イオンの部分電荷と変位の積を足す方法は、分極の直感的な見積もりには使えるが、 "
"周期結晶の分極を厳密に評価するには電子状態を含む扱いが必要である（\\ :ref:`分極の評価<polarization-"
"evaluation>`）。したがって、 構造図や :math:`c/a` のみから分極の値を断定しない。"
msgstr ""
"Summing products of ionic partial charges and displacements gives an "
"intuitive estimate of the polarization, but a rigorous evaluation in a "
"periodic crystal must include the electronic state (see \\ "
":ref:`evaluation of polarization <polarization-evaluation>`). Therefore, "
"do not infer a definite polarization value from a structure diagram or "
"from :math:`c/a` alone."

